      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The purpose of this work was to determine current practices of pediatric surgeons in the management of community peritonitis, excepting antibiotic use and resuscitation car. A questionnaire was sent to 63 French pediatric surgeons in France. Forty-six answers concerning appendicular peritonitis were analyzed. Laparoscopy was a good indication for 40 surgeons. A sample for bacteriological examination was never ordered. Conditions for washing and drainage were detailed. Treatment to prevent postoperative pain was used by all."},
